WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.850
The plan has seven actions.

2
00:00:01.850 --> 00:00:04.813
Create means the policy
isn't in the tenant yet,

3
00:00:04.813 --> 00:00:07.075
and it's always created report-only.

4
00:00:07.075 --> 00:00:11.451
Update means it differs, and the patch
carries only the changed top-level

5
00:00:11.451 --> 00:00:15.900
properties, as Microsoft Learn's
reference for updating a policy advises.

6
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.737
NoChange means it matches.

7
00:00:17.737 --> 00:00:22.071
Blocked means it needs an authentication
strength or a context the

8
00:00:22.071 --> 00:00:26.326
tenant doesn't have yet, and the next
run, once that exists, creates it.

9
00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:28.379
Held means the file says enabled,

10
00:00:28.379 --> 00:00:31.575
the tenant doesn't, and you
didn't pass Allow Enforce.

11
00:00:31.575 --> 00:00:36.225
Differs is a strength that differs,
because the code doesn't update strengths.

12
00:00:36.225 --> 00:00:40.813
And NotInRepository is a policy in
the tenant that isn't in the files.

13
00:00:40.813 --> 00:00:42.987
It's reported, and never deleted.

14
00:00:42.987 --> 00:00:47.590
A dry run writes the plan and the requests
it would send, and sends nothing.
